ne and sends his army  out to conquer the north  that's when Sentra burns and house Aden  becomes the site of the mages Last Stand  amazingly the mages managed to hold  sodden until help arrives from one of  the northern kingdoms you know that King  who arrives riding a white horse with an  army behind him  that's King full test of tomaría and if  that name sounds familiar it should  you've met him before king foltest is  the same King Geralt met at betrayer  moon he's the one who slept with his  sister who then died and gave birth to  the Striga that Geralt had  white bull test shows up thanks to Tris  miracle the mage assigned to his core to  fought at the Battle of sodden the King  still owes Tris for helping Geralt save  his daughter and it's just too bad that  he took a sweet time getting there much  more ends on a couple of cliffhangers  ciri and Geralt meet for the first time  and more importantly yennefer seems to  have disappeared after unleashing some  major magic on the nilfgaardian army  yennefer more or less vanishes the last  we hear of her to saya is worriedly  calling out her name given that much  more clearly establishes that using  powerful magic can kill a person it's  cause for alarm still don't worry too  much  yennefer is a major player in the books  and unless the show is planning to  deviate pretty radically from the source  material the sorceress should pop up in  season two and might take a little while  but we're almost certain she'll be there  while yennefer is defending the north  from milk guards advance Geralt spends  most of the season finale lying in the  back of a hay cart suffering poison  induced flashbacks to his past the  biggest revelation to come out of those  visions is at the Sena  a sorceress raised Geralt when he was a  small boy in fact while the show doesn't  make an entirely clear Witcher lore  dictates that the Sena is Geralt  biological mother the Sena didn't take  care of Geralt for long though when he  was still young she abandoned him  leaving him to be taken to care morin  where witcher's live in her train and  much more Geralt comes face to face with  his mother for the first time in decades  in a scene that could be magic or just a  hallucination whether the Sena actually  came to visit Geralt or nods you can  expect more details about the witcher's  childhood it's season 2 don't ask any  more questions or the answers will only  hurt us both  it's time to move on down the other  major figure introduced in Geralt  visions is vesemir after the Sena  disappears it's vesemir who comes to  little Geralt sate and garel utters his  name a few times during his poison  induced delirium The Witcher doesn't  explain who vesemir is but fans of the  franchise know him quite well like Daryl  vesemir is a Witcher he lives at the  Witcher stronghold Kerr Morin and is one  of the oldest and most respected members  of the fraternity thanks to a past  adventure gone awry vesemir rarely  leaves Kerr Morin however he's one of  the best instructors the witcher's have  and he functions as a de facto father  figure to Geralt in the books the show  will probably make a few changes to the  story but the season finale has already  put the basic pieces in place expect  vesemir to pop up during season two  ultimately the first season of The  Witcher is about three people trying to  find a family we don't know one until a  finale but the Geralt we meet at the  beginning of the show was abandoned by  his mother  yennefer is sold off by her foster  father and deprived of the ability to  have children series family is killed in  the very first episode each one of these  characters has the opportunity to find a  new family over the course of the season  and each one rejects it instead our  three heroes find comfort in each other  in the books the trio form a makeshift  family the show isn't quite there yet  but if you're paying attention it's very  clear where it's going check out one of  our newest videos